\begin_layout Subsubsection
Attack 3:
 Replayed packets
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Here,
 the attacker has somehow captured a legitimate packet and replayed it.
 In this demonstration,
 I recorded packets using my 
\family typewriter
listen_udp.py
\family default
 diagnostic script,
 and inserted one into the attacker's Python code.
 A more clever hacker who positioned themselves on the network and ran some capture software such as WireShark might be able to intercept packets.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Regardless of how the legitimate packet was captured,
 my system rejects it because it is received 
\shape italic
out of order
\shape default
.
 The packets are not encrypted,
 so this kind of attack is still possible.
 Nevertheless the gateway rejects the out-of-order packet,
 while allowing legitimate packets through.
\end_layout

